We are looking for a DevOps / Cloud Infrastructure Engineer for service agreement collaboration (B2B contract) to cooperate with a team that connects Flix's cloud platform with the new train fleet. &nbsp;

This is a contractor engagement for a DevOps / Cloud Infrastructure professional who wants to work on impactful, hands-on challenges with real technical depth and a lot of cross-company collaboration. &nbsp;

Scope of Services &nbsp;

You will help shape an architecture from the start, make sure it is secure and reliable, and take it all the way to production. &nbsp;

About the Engagement &nbsp;

• Design, build and operate the cloud infrastructure that connects onboard train systems with Flix's backend services, covering telemetry ingestion, alerting, video streams and remote content delivery &nbsp;

• Build and maintain the infrastructure-as-code foundation of the platform, keeping the Terraform/Terragrunt codebase clean, scalable and easy for others to work with &nbsp;

• Steer technical proposals and topics across backend and infrastructure, from the first idea and design discussion to a working solution in production &nbsp;

• Take part in system design and architecture discussions and constructively challenge architectural decisions when you see a better path &nbsp;

• Define and implement secure communication between the trains and the cloud, including mTLS, certificate management and network design &nbsp;

• Work closely with train manufacturers’ engineers to agree on interfaces, protocols and responsibilities on both sides of the integration &nbsp;

• Collaborate with backend developers and other Flix teams so that new services are deployed reliably and are easy to run and monitor &nbsp;

• Make sure the platform is reliable, observable and secure, so that we know what is happening in our systems before our users do &nbsp;

About You &nbsp;

• Solid hands-on experience in infrastructure engineering and in designing and running cloud environments &nbsp;

• Experience with AWS (preferred). Experience with any other major cloud platform is also welcome &nbsp;

• Strong knowledge of Terraform/Terragrunt for infrastructure provisioning and automation &nbsp;

• A solid understanding of systems architecture and system design, and the confidence to challenge architectural decisions with clear arguments &nbsp;

• Good knowledge of networking, including mTLS and SSL/TLS &nbsp;

• Foundational knowledge of security and the ability to apply it in everyday infrastructure decisions &nbsp;

• Proven ability to lead technical proposals and topics across backend and infrastructure, and to bring your stakeholders along with you &nbsp;

• Strong critical thinking, including the ability to analyze a problem, weigh trade-offs and explain your reasoning clearly &nbsp;

Nice to have: &nbsp;

• Experience with IoT, automotive, or other remote device integrations &nbsp;

• Experience as a backend engineer or full-stack developer, ideally in the JVM ecosystem &nbsp;

• Familiarity with Linux and virtual machines &nbsp;

Collaboration Model &nbsp;

• Contract type: Cooperation based on a service agreement (B2B/freelance contract), not an employment contract &nbsp;

• Working model: Independent contractor responsible for delivering agreed services and submitting invoices &nbsp;

